@title BliztSite Web Syntax Sample
@description A full sample covering the current BliztSite Web language features.

h1: BliztSite Web
p: This sample shows [strong:headings], [em:inline emphasis], [code:inline code], and a [link:link to About|/about.html].

h2: Paragraphs and line breaks
p: You can write plain paragraph lines and insert a manual break here.[br]This text appears on the next line.

h3: Lists
li: First item
li: Second item with [strong:bold text]
li: Third item with [em:italic text]
li: Fourth item with [code:npx blizt build]
li: Fifth item with a [link:homepage|/]

h4: Quotes
quote: Keep the syntax tiny, readable, and easy to turn into HTML.

h5: Fallback plain text
This line has no prefix, so Blizt treats it as a normal paragraph.

h6: Code block
code:
const site = "Blizt";
const extension = ".bsw";

function build() {
  console.log(`Building ${site} pages from ${extension} files`);
}
end

h2: Raw HTML block
html:
<section class="feature-card">
  <h3>Embedded HTML</h3>
  <p>This block is passed through directly.</p>
</section>
end

p: End of sample.
